hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"249","On blood-money, concerning a Muslim being executed for a disbeliever he killed: [Ibn Abi Najiyah] al-Iskandarani narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Sulayman [ibn Bilal] narrated to me, Rabi'ah narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Baylamani; he narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a Muslim man who had killed a covenanted person of the dhimmah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) brought the Muslim forward and his neck was struck, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the worthiest to fulfill his covenant. Ibn Wahb said: Its explanation is that he killed him treacherously."
"250","[Wahb ibn Bayan, Ahmad ibn Sa'id al-Hamadhani, and Ibn al-Sarh said:] Ibn Wahb informed us, Abdullah ibn Ya'qub informed me; Abdullah ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Salih al-Hadrami narrated to us, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) killed, on the day of Khaybar, a Muslim for a disbeliever he had killed treacherously, and said: I am the worthiest - or most entitled - to fulfill his covenant."
